## Summary

Restore the logical-warp/vectorized `silu_and_mul_per_block_quant` implementation from #44173, which was reverted by #45066 after a ROCm wave64 mask-width build failure.

This version incorporates the ROCm-safe half-wave mask developed in #45055 and preserves the later int64 token-offset fix from #53409:

- one logical 32-lane warp per `(token, group)`;
- four groups per 128-thread block;
- vectorized gate/up loads and quantized stores;
- shuffle reduction without shared memory or `__syncthreads`;
- a 32-bit CUDA mask and 64-bit, half-wave-selecting ROCm mask.

The implementation and commit retain attribution to the original optimization and ROCm fix authors. This is intended as a current-main, single-commit successor to the conflicted Draft #45055, not as unrelated new work.

